      "reason": "'率' (ritsu) is a much more general and appropriate translation for the English noun 'rate', covering meanings such as 'rate', 'ratio', 'proportion', and 'percentage'. It is commonly used as a standalone noun or as a suffix to form compound words for various types of rates (e.g., 利率 'interest rate', 死亡率 'death rate')."
